# AUTHORED-BY Claude Opus 5.5
# Node-level composition for the exported validation shape (./health.shacl.ttl).
# SHACL targets do not inherit, so a node typed only health:StepCountObservation,
# health:SleepObservation or health:HeartRateObservation is not a focus node of
# hsh:ObservationShape. The federation health sector composes its subtype shapes
# with `sh:node hsh:ObservationShape` so the Observation MUSTs (code, patient,
# effective time, value, UCUM unit) still apply.
# federation-codegen admission rejects that composition in codegen/health.shapes.ttl
# ("sh:node: no runtime projection"), and rejects repeating the Observation
# property constraints on the subtype shapes ("field claims a runtime structural
# predicate"). The generated runtime already enforces the Observation composite
# when it parses a subtype; only the exported SHACL artefact lacked it.
# scripts/build-shacl.mjs therefore merges src/generated/shapes.ttl with exactly
# these triples (parsed with n3, written with n3.Writer) into dist/health.shacl.ttl.
# Every subject and object must be a NodeShape of the generated shapes, and only
# sh:node is allowed here; the build fails otherwise. Generator gap: tracker
# inbox note personal-connectors-codegen-node-composition (parent epic sst-ild).
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix hsh: <https://jeswr.org/ns/sectors/health/import-shapes#> .

hsh:HeartRateShape sh:node hsh:ObservationShape .
hsh:StepsShape sh:node hsh:ObservationShape .
hsh:SleepShape sh:node hsh:ObservationShape .
